// The same allow rule as policy.rego.example / policy.yaml.example,
// expressed in Cedar. See README.md "Policy backends".
//
// Known limitation: Cedar has no float or null type, and a bounded
// Long integer range. Tool-call params containing a JSON float, null,
// or an out-of-range integer will be denied (fail-closed) rather than
// coerced -- this is deliberate, not a bug. See README.md "Policy
// backends" for details.
permit(
  principal == Wardline::Identity::"agent-abc123",
  action == Wardline::Action::"call_tool",
  resource == Wardline::Tool::"read_file"
);
